From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] uri2pem: exit non-zero on verification failure

When --verify is used and the OpenSSL pkey verification fails,
exit with a non-zero status code so that callers can detect the
failure programmatically.

Previously the script would print a failure message but always
exit 0, making it impossible for build systems to catch
inaccessible PKCS#11 keys early.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [OE-specific]

Signed-off-by: Chris Trowbridge <chris.trowbridge@ezurio.com>
---
 tools/uri2pem.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/tools/uri2pem.py b/tools/uri2pem.py
index 1111111..2222222 100755
--- a/tools/uri2pem.py
+++ b/tools/uri2pem.py
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ if __name__ == "__main__":
         ret = subprocess.run(["openssl", "pkey", "-in", str(out_file), "-pubout"])
         print("===== END =====")
         if ret.returncode != 0:
             print(f"{sys.argv[0]}: verification of private key PEM({str(out_file)}) failed")
+            sys.exit(1)
         else:
             print(f"{sys.argv[0]}: verification of private key PEM({str(out_file)}) OK")
 
